Z||000006||1FST2M6||06-18-2000||10:06 PM||||toyota = VVT-i  <P>now that the patent has run out on Honda EVERYONE is getting in the valve timing game. Saab has had a similar idea but realized there is more power to be found in variable compression heads... they thought of this back in the late 80s and are just now letting everone know about it. There is also somthing that has been around for a while in Toyota and Alfa Romeo - additional intake runners... the Corolla GT-S back in the AE-86 model had another set of runners allowing more air to come in the motor at a given RPM. Alfas Milano 3.0 had this same thing. just one more thing to think about... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-18-2000).]||||reg||1
